From 7e858dc6cfc1363c630f8d08a622a38e2f170946 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devandroid-bit <180217512+Devandroid-bit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:09:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] BACKPORT: zram: support multiple compression streams

Backport the zram multi-compression feature to the Exynos9820 4.14
tree. A zram device can now have one primary and up to three secondary
compression algorithms, configured through recomp_algorithm. Existing
pages can be recompressed in place with the recompress attribute
(type=idle|huge|huge_idle, optional threshold and algo), and the
per-page compression priority is tracked in the zram table flags.

Adapted for the Samsung 4.14 zram driver:
- keep ZRAM_FLAG_SHIFT at 24 and store the priority in two spare flag
  bits after ZRAM_LRU;
- preserve the Samsung LRU/idle writeback state when recompressing an
  object instead of calling zram_free_page();
- do not write recompressed objects to the compressed backing device,
  because its on-disk header has no room for the compression priority;
  such objects stay in zsmalloc;
- add zs_lookup_class_index() from the upstream series.

CONFIG_ZRAM_MULTI_COMP is enabled in the d1, d1xks, d2s, d2x and d2xks
configurations. No new option is needed in exynos9820_defconfig because
the device fragments are merged after it.

Backported from: mainline v6.2 zram multi-compression series, also
present in Google ACK android15-6.6 and android16-6.12; not present in
Galaxy S24 6.1 (S921BXXSGDZG1).

