From fb9c6c1c8ec305e09f26f43bee5e382fc52c77ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devandroid-bit <180217512+Devandroid-bit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:22:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] BACKPORT: f2fs: support age threshold based garbage
 collection

Backport the ATGC (age-threshold GC) victim selection policy to the
Exynos9820 4.14 F2FS driver.

When the atgc mount option is set and the filesystem is older than
7 days, background GC uses GC_AT: dirty sections are collected into an
rbtree ordered by section mtime, and the victim is chosen by a cost
derived from section age and valid-block count instead of the
cost-benefit or greedy algorithms. The age threshold, candidate ratio,
candidate count and age weight are tunable at runtime through
/sys/fs/f2fs/<dev>/atgc_*.

Backported from: Galaxy S24 6.1 (S921BXXSGDZG1), based on upstream
v5.11 commit 093749e296e2 ("f2fs: support age threshold based garbage
collection") and follow-up 89e53ff1651a ("f2fs: atgc: fix to set
default age threshold").

Adapted for the Samsung 4.14 tree:
- port only the GC_AT victim-selection path; the AT_SSR (age-threshold
  SSR and inmem curseg) machinery from the same series is omitted
  because this tree has no curseg->seg_type, NR_CURSEG_INMEM_TYPE or
  f2fs_save_inmem_curseg()/f2fs_load_inmem_curseg() infrastructure.
  Without AT_SSR, GC'd data keeps using CURSEG_COLD_DATA and SSR keeps
  its existing policy; GC_AT itself is unaffected.
- use a local mtime-keyed rbtree lookup helper because the 4.14
  rb_entry layout (extent_cache) differs from the upstream one.
- set sbi->gc_mode to GC_IDLE_AT in the sysfs gc_idle handler; the
  upstream v5.11 patch stored the GC_AT policy value there, which
  aliases GC_IDLE_GREEDY in the sb gc_mode enum.
- add 64-bit show/store handling for atgc_age_threshold.

There is no gc_urgent_sleep_thread knob in upstream F2FS or in this
tree; the existing gc_urgent_sleep_time control is left unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Devandroid-bit <180217512+Devandroid-bit@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: @Devandroid-bit.
